# Scoped exception to the global USE="-introspection" (make.conf.tmpl) — the ONE
# flag flip that makes net-firewall/firewalld (a REQUESTED atom, packages.list)
# resolvable at all. The hard chain, identical at EVERY firewalld version in the
# tree (2.4.0/2.4.2/2.4.4 all RDEPEND dev-python/pygobject:3 — firewalld is a
# python daemon, so no version pin can dodge this):
#
#   net-firewall/firewalld
#     -> dev-python/pygobject:3
#       -> dev-libs/gobject-introspection
#         -> >=dev-libs/glib-2.82.0:2[introspection]   <- satisfied by this file
#
# Without it the 2026-07-30 21:04 mesh build died on ALL THREE rpi5 roles:
#   emerge: there are no ebuilds built with USE flags to satisfy
#   ">=dev-libs/glib-2.82.0:2[introspection]" for /out/wl-pki.rpi5/sysroot/.
# and the requested-atom completeness gate then (correctly) refused the images
# ("1 requested package(s) are NOT installed: net-firewall/firewalld").
# Dropping firewalld from packages.list instead is NOT acceptable — that is the
# exact hole the completeness gate exists to close (firewalld-less rpi5 images
# once shipped silently; see tests/build-arm-payload-gates.sh's header).
#
# THE COMPILE-SIDE BET, stated plainly: resolution probes on the real failed
# sysroots prove the DEPGRAPH closes with this line (rc=0, firewalld in the
# plan, zero new USE/keyword walls — FINDINGS.md on fix/arm-firewalld-installable);
# they CANNOT prove glib COMPILES cross. Enabling glib[introspection] re-arms
# glib's bundled gobject-introspection BOOTSTRAP during cross src_configure —
# the very thing the -introspection comment in make.conf.tmpl records as broken
# (bc87d1e / PR #163: "ImportError: _giscanner.cpython-314-...so" — g-ir-scanner
# under host python 3.14, extension built for PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET python3_12,
# glib-2.86 era). What has changed since that recording:
#   (a) the python skew is GONE — the arm64 seed ships python3_14 only and the
#       rendered make.conf pins PYTHON_TARGETS/PYTHON_SINGLE_TARGET=python3_14,
#       matching the build host's python;
#   (b) the current tree's meson.eclass writes a cross exe_wrapper from
#       sysroot.eclass's sysroot_make_run_prefixed — a qemu-aarch64 wrapper that
#       SELF-TESTS (compiles and runs a target exe) before meson trusts it, and
#       build-rpi5-stage4.sh refuses to start without static qemu-aarch64 +
#       binfmt_misc registered;
#   (c) glib is 2.88.2, two bumps past the recorded 2.86 failure.
# The first real rpi5 build after this change is the compile-side proof. If the
# bootstrap still dies there, the runtime backstop is unchanged — the
# completeness gate fails the build loudly naming firewalld — and the recorded
# fallback is a documented, per-platform, operator-decided exclusion (candidate
# C in FINDINGS.md), never a silent skip.
#
# Gate-time twin: tests/requested-atoms-resolvable.sh fails the moment this
# scoped override is dropped while the global -introspection wall stands, so
# the regression class (a global USE mask silently making a requested atom
# unresolvable) is caught at gate time, not at hour N of a real build.
#
# Deliberately glib-ONLY: gobject-introspection and pygobject carry no
# 'introspection' flag of their own, and the global -introspection/-vala stay
# authoritative for the rest of the image. Marginal cost measured on the real
# sysroots: 3 package actions (glib USE-rebuild + gobject-introspection +
# gobject-introspection-common). pygobject's default +cairo chain is inherent
# to firewalld's pygobject dep, not to this line ('dev-python/pygobject -cairo'
# is a separate lean-image candidate, deliberately NOT bundled into this fix).
dev-libs/glib introspection
